.TH COMMANDS 1 "September 2026" "ProwseTk" "Prowse-TUI Help"
.SH NAME
commands \- navigation, automation, and export
.SH NAVIGATION
.TP
.B :open URL
Navigate to an HTTP(S) URL through the live session.
.TP
.B :follow N
Follow a numbered link in the rendered browser page.
.TP
.B :back
Navigate to the previous URL.
.TP
.B :reload
Reload the current URL.
.TP
.B :top / :bottom
Move to the first or last browser line.
.TP
.B :bookmark / :bookmarks
Add an in-memory bookmark or list bookmarks.
.SH AUTOMATION
.TP
.B :lua CODE
Execute Lua against the managed global session.
.TP
.B :source FILE
Load and execute a Lua script in the current runtime.
.TP
.B :driver FILE
Execute a Lua file and call main with an empty argument table.
Drivers must return zero. Drivers that create their own sessions remain isolated;
use global session to manipulate the visible page.
.TP
.B :select CSS
Inspect matching elements.
.TP
.B :click CSS
Dispatch a synthetic click on the first matching element.
.TP
.B :set CSS VALUE
Type a value into the first matching control. The selector cannot contain spaces.
.SH EXPORT
.TP
.B :links / :urls FILE
List or save redacted resolved links and resource URLs.
.TP
.B :endpoints FILE
Save heuristic OpenAPI endpoint discovery with provenance and redaction.
Coverage is incomplete; inferred endpoints are not authoritative.
.TP
.B :text FILE
Save visible page text. Page content may include private information.
.SH OTHER
:find REGEX searches the browser page. :config opens settings. :quit exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR search 1
.MR config 1
.MR extensions 1
